meta {
  name: 409
  seq: 4
}

script:pre-request {
  await bru.runRequest("Get Authentication Token");
  const startApplicationRes = await bru.runRequest("Applications/Start Application");
  bru.setVar("applicationId", startApplicationRes.data.id);
}

docs {
  # 409 Conflict (ETag Mismatch)

  Covers every update endpoint that takes an `eTag` in its request body. The folder's
  pre-request script (above) runs **Get Token** and then the shared **Applications/Start
  Application** to create a fresh application (whose eTag always starts at `0`), storing its id
  in the `applicationId` runtime variable. Each request then sends a deliberately mismatched
  `"eTag": 999` in the body, asserting `409 Conflict`.

  ⚠️ See the collection-level docs for the caveat about `GlobalExceptionHandler` being disabled
  under the `local` Spring profile (i.e. `make docker-up`), which turns this 409 into a 500.
}
